WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:13,500
You mentioned genetics, and some of the people that I've talked to have said that in terms

00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:19,320
of cancer, genetics plays a much smaller role than many people think, maybe sometimes

00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:20,320
less than 20%.

00:00:20,320 --> 00:00:22,820
Well, it depends on what they're talking about.

00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:29,740
So when I look at genetics, and I look at it, did this person have a gene that causes cancer?

00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:30,740
No.

00:00:30,740 --> 00:00:32,340
I don't believe that exists.

00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:38,420
There are tumor suppressor genes that if I have defects on those genes, then my tumor

00:00:38,420 --> 00:00:41,900
suppressor pathway is going to be suppressed.

00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:49,020
So what that means is that normally, if I have a cell in my body that something inside

00:00:49,020 --> 00:00:54,820
that cell disrupts the replication cycle, and it starts to replicate, but you have protective

00:00:54,820 --> 00:01:00,060
measures, these genetic protective measures, that are called tumor suppressor pathways.

00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:05,140
So normally, those should be signaled and turned on and cause a poptosis in that cell.

00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:12,220
But if I have a defect on that pathway, that won't turn on, or it won't turn on as strongly,

00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:15,380
and I'm going to be more susceptible to cancer.

00:01:15,380 --> 00:01:20,020
To me, I don't ever believe that that is the cause of the cancer, something the tumor suppressor

00:01:20,020 --> 00:01:26,620
gene defect didn't cause the replication to start happening in the cell, something else

00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:29,140
had to take place there.

00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:34,580
But if I have a bunch of defects on specific tumor suppressor pathways, I could be more

00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:39,380
susceptible to getting cancer if that starts to replicate.

00:01:39,380 --> 00:01:43,860
So, but that's not what we're looking at so much when we're looking at genes, we're looking

00:01:43,860 --> 00:01:52,460
at how the detox pathways that I spoke about, and what you look at other pathways, you can

00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:58,260
tell what could possibly feed the cancer, because cancer has to have a fuel source.

00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:06,500
So when you look at specific genetic pathways, you can see, okay, they have defects on this gene

00:02:06,500 --> 00:02:11,180
and this gene and this gene and this gene, then they're going to have excess this product,

00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:17,460
this byproduct, because it's not converting to substance B, is that byproduct of potential

00:02:17,460 --> 00:02:23,500
fuel for cancer, if it is, then boy, that could be definitely a fuel line for cancer.

00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:27,580
So looking at that, then you can support that pathway or change that person's diet based

00:02:27,580 --> 00:02:28,580
to put it there.

